{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:50:04.053150Z","id":"3de8bfad05e1e7bda9ab909952d90fbff3bbe569edc8b37fef5a835fcfd468d3","body":{"detail":"The check read every file of the home, remote.key (32 random bytes) included, as lossy UTF-8 and asserted it did not contain \"cx\", meant as a token prefix (cxg_). Random key bytes hold \"cx\" with probability about 31/65536 per run, so `just test` failed now and then in //crates/clax-cli:integration__3 with \"remote.key holds a token\". The check now looks for the issued token itself, which no other file can hold by chance.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":228},"end":{"line":235},"content_hash":"f03107e3547e8a2fe801e40610e53916f3d9692fb036e053cca927422a04d9ec"},"summary":"connect_with_an_invite_writes_remote_json_and_key_0600 failed by chance: it asserted no file but remote.json contains \"cx\"","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:50:57.089720Z","id":"2e85f32b9ab8eeb246c997bbfd72aa29f6b9e841626211b7ddea10b67ee051ba","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cac3e947beb931234ea53e1bac1c00e29fa3e117","summary":"Fixed in git:cac3e947: the check looks for the issued token, which no other file holds by chance; bazel test //crates/clax-cli:integration__3 --test_arg=connect_with_an_invite_writes_remote_json_and_key_0600: PASSED","supersedes":"3de8bfad05e1e7bda9ab909952d90fbff3bbe569edc8b37fef5a835fcfd468d3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/tests/switch.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:57:44.371106Z","id":"9dc929b1de92d48ac6e71695d32b61c76c319ce7102c621c44602fbf96a7ca7b","body":{"detail":"Failure: one run of bazelisk test //crates/clax-cli:integration__2 failed at line 222, assert_eq!(v[\"port\"], fake.port): left 61131, right 61130. The new daemon took the next port, as if the replaced daemon's port was still held when it bound (port_held probes 127.0.0.1 and [::1]), while the next run of the same target passed. The test, the serve command and clax_core::daemon are as on main.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":206},"end":{"line":224},"content_hash":"cbb24bbdf0ec4dcaaa015dff82f87d0c2ec7aab76c286bb9f1be986060e1bfec"},"summary":"The replacing daemon sometimes listens on the port after the replaced daemon's, not on its port","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/tests/follow.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:57:46.223396Z","id":"a32a302271701f7190d4f5d9360254c19f9d5310e7350eb715d39e7763f5641a","body":{"detail":"it_survives_a_daemon_restart (line 321), it_exits_cleanly_when_the_session_ends (349), it_exits_at_once_when_a_followed_clax_session_ends (360), once_exits_after_the_first_poll_that_printed (414) and once_exits_cleanly_when_the_session_ends (441) each sleep 500 ms and assume the spawned `clax feedback follow` has made its first poll by then. Under load a freshly started binary can take longer (crates/clax-cli/tests/switch.rs:177-178 notes that one can take a second to launch). The test then races the follower's start-up: for example, the session ends before the follower has resolved it. Line 364 asserts `ended.elapsed() < Duration::from_secs(3)`, a wall-clock budget. once_does_not_exit_on_an_empty_poll sleeps a fixed 3 s (line 465). AGENTS.md forbids both: no sleeps standing in for a condition, no wall-clock budgets in any check.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":305},"end":{"line":466},"content_hash":"1522c43940e46d120cf7e66b02e0e16bbdecfcafcb6692fce99d82b6f6253dc8"},"suggested_fix":"Have the follower signal readiness: a line on stderr, or a daemon-side count of polls for the session that the test waits on with a deadline. Wait on that instead of sleeping. Drop the elapsed() assertion; f.exit(Duration::from_secs(3)) already bounds the wait. For the 'does not exit on an empty poll' case, wait until the daemon has answered two polls rather than for 3 s.","summary":"The follower tests sleep 500 ms in place of waiting for the follower to start polling, assert a wall-clock bound, and idle 3 s to show the follower keeps running","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/tests/follow.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:30.507449Z","id":"d53e720936d55b4da4d3a45fca46fbc2e066bd81d3652154689fd140872460ab","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-cli/tests/follow.rs:321, 349, 360, 414, 441 each std::thread::sleep(500 ms) after Follower::spawn before acting on the daemon; line 364 asserts `ended.elapsed() < Duration::from_secs(3)`; line 465 sleeps 3 s before checking the follower still runs. crates/clax-cli/tests/switch.rs:177-178 documents that a freshly built binary can take a second to launch. AGENTS.md ('Code') forbids sleeps standing in for a condition and wall-clock budgets in any check. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"a32a302271701f7190d4f5d9360254c19f9d5310e7350eb715d39e7763f5641a","summary":"confirmed: the follower tests sleep in place of a readiness signal and assert a wall-clock bound","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/tests/follow.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:59:20.642339Z","id":"3ff74ba890f169ba1d0122a62916fa06a92ad5a5a97c3a8e996fe1ee26f86073","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2e580ac54","summary":"Fixed: the follower tests wait for the follower's first poll instead of sleeping, with no wall-clock bound; //crates/clax-cli/... pass.","supersedes":"a32a302271701f7190d4f5d9360254c19f9d5310e7350eb715d39e7763f5641a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/tests/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:36:39.664353Z","id":"b00f8b2f3c93f8a1f102095e7523768bb36d8c0cf2f5ae193b1b08864dac47ba","body":{"detail":"Failure: in CI runs 39196046933, 39265231518, 39176670949 and 39284215858, //crates/clax-cli:integration__2 failed bin_shows_sets_and_clears_the_binary_the_plugins_run (line 66) and init_points_the_bin_setting_at_this_binary_and_uninit_removes_it (line 139): stdout named .../execroot/_main/bazel-out/k8-fastbuild/bin/crates/clax-cli/clax where the test expected .../sandbox/linux-sandbox/<n>/execroot/.../integration__2.runfiles/_main/crates/clax-cli/clax. Deterministic under the Linux sandbox, not a load flake.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":62},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"5eca67dfbeae731cdcf6a7d1d3846f3f56974757304e14f866bdb047189902e6"},"summary":"bin set --this and init name the binary by its resolved execroot path in CI's Linux sandbox, not the runfiles path the tests expect","tags":["tests","ci","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/tests/cli.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:36:39.664666Z","id":"5e69750586dc2457b6b53ee37030410fa09d0e65f0ed8628fbafa27bd0d95379","body":{"detail":"Failure: in CI runs 39196046933, 39176698604, 39176670949 and 39440289806, //crates/clax-cli:integration__1 panicked in this test (cli.rs:1015 then, 1190 now); the hooks.log line names bin=.../execroot/_main/bazel-out/k8-fastbuild/bin/crates/clax-cli/clax. Likely the same resolved-path difference as the bin.rs tests (crates/clax-cli/tests/bin.rs:62-66).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1172},"end":{"line":1195},"content_hash":"cb0ba70ae0728fb0fcce645b5434ffdecdf3ad55a6f86bd3fbc5cb65422922bd"},"summary":"every_hook_run_appends_a_line_to_hooks_log fails in CI: the logged bin= path is not the one the test expects","tags":["tests","ci","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/tests/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T16:40:20.684447Z","id":"d37313172a496d62006b03af94bd27f683357f6d1aedf64a9b60003bf2766796","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b00f8b2f3c93f8a1f102095e7523768bb36d8c0cf2f5ae193b1b08864dac47ba","summary":"ab776ae12 compares through crates/clax-cli/tests/common/mod.rs as_clax, which writes the canonical path of the test binary as the path the tests run. Cause: std::env::current_exe resolves symbolic links on Linux (/proc/self/exe) and not on macOS, and Bazel's runfiles path is a link. bazelisk test //crates/clax-cli:integration__1 __2 __3 pass on macOS; not yet run on Linux, so this stays open until a Linux CI run passes.","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/tests/cli.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T16:40:20.741698Z","id":"977f79c0ca3a4bb9228854cd9eb61d664ecd354c84c04225851f913d8dd68657","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5e69750586dc2457b6b53ee37030410fa09d0e65f0ed8628fbafa27bd0d95379","summary":"ab776ae12 compares through crates/clax-cli/tests/common/mod.rs as_clax, which writes the canonical path of the test binary as the path the tests run. Cause: std::env::current_exe resolves symbolic links on Linux (/proc/self/exe) and not on macOS, and Bazel's runfiles path is a link. bazelisk test //crates/clax-cli:integration__1 __2 __3 pass on macOS; not yet run on Linux, so this stays open until a Linux CI run passes.","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/tests/cli.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:48.395763Z","id":"7458c64b7e12ad15364b41d98a44c92ce647ac8cc132f72cd3740df4851828fb","body":{"detail":"Failure: in CI runs 39196046933, 39176698604, 39176670949 and 39440289806, //crates/clax-cli:integration__1 panicked in this test (cli.rs:1015 then, 1190 now); the hooks.log line names bin=.../execroot/_main/bazel-out/k8-fastbuild/bin/crates/clax-cli/clax. Likely the same resolved-path difference as the bin.rs tests (crates/clax-cli/tests/bin.rs:62-66).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1184},"end":{"line":1209},"content_hash":"74b77f52b18e23bb55e91486593840082cbc1f95b8fa1405aa5b290529ae27a1"},"summary":"every_hook_run_appends_a_line_to_hooks_log fails in CI: the logged bin= path is not the one the test expects","supersedes":"5e69750586dc2457b6b53ee37030410fa09d0e65f0ed8628fbafa27bd0d95379","tags":["tests","ci","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/tests/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:39:12.706816Z","id":"b2671eff9bb3bd09eb8930fdb8649054a29df0bf78236f800eab0228684ad87f","body":{"detail":"Failure: in CI runs 39196046933, 39265231518, 39176670949 and 39284215858, //crates/clax-cli:integration__2 failed bin_shows_sets_and_clears_the_binary_the_plugins_run (line 66) and init_points_the_bin_setting_at_this_binary_and_uninit_removes_it (line 139): stdout named .../execroot/_main/bazel-out/k8-fastbuild/bin/crates/clax-cli/clax where the test expected .../sandbox/linux-sandbox/<n>/execroot/.../integration__2.runfiles/_main/crates/clax-cli/clax. Deterministic under the Linux sandbox, not a load flake.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"6e3384807e1f152224c73dd2d014c85bb44a185c34020f4b90ac7f1b4f6409e6"},"summary":"bin set --this and init name the binary by its resolved execroot path in CI's Linux sandbox, not the runfiles path the tests expect","supersedes":"b00f8b2f3c93f8a1f102095e7523768bb36d8c0cf2f5ae193b1b08864dac47ba","tags":["tests","ci","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
